course: dictionary
lesson: 12848
title: Formal words: endeavour
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Endeavour is a formal word. It is used in serious writing, school reports and exams. As a noun it means a serious effort or attempt. «Her latest endeavour was building a model bridge.» Here endeavour is a thing she tried to do, and the words serious and building are your clues.
explain: As a verb, endeavour means to try hard to do something. «We endeavour to help every pupil.» Check the meaning by swapping in try: «We try hard to help every pupil» still makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: Endeavour can also mean hard work towards a goal. «Human endeavour has sent people into space.» Look out for phrases such as «make every endeavour» and «in all your endeavours», which are common in formal writing.
fact: «Endeavour» means a serious effort, or to try hard to do something.
fact: «Endeavour» is a formal word, so you will often see it in serious writing, school reports and exams.
fact: Useful phrases: «endeavour to», «in all your endeavours», «human endeavour», «make every endeavour».
fact: Captain Cook's ship was called the Endeavour, and space endeavours are serious efforts in space science.
fact: To check a meaning, swap in «try» or «effort». If the sentence still makes sense, you have it right.
exercise: «Her endeavour to learn the piano took three years.» What does endeavour mean here? | A small room with a piano | *A serious effort to do something | A loud noise | A quick nap
exercise: «We endeavour to help every pupil.» What does endeavour mean in this sentence? | Sing very loudly | Forget all about it | *Try hard to do something | Stop trying
exercise: What was the name of Captain Cook's ship? | Victory | Titanic | Mayflower | *Endeavour
test: «Jo made every endeavour to finish the race.» What is the best meaning of endeavour? | A kind of cloud | A short sleep | A dinner at a restaurant | *Hard effort to reach a goal
test: Which sentence uses endeavour as a verb, a doing word? | «Her endeavour was long and hard.» | «The new endeavour is very exciting.» | *«We endeavour to be kind to everyone.» | «The endeavour sat on the shelf.»
exam: Which word is the best synonym for endeavour in «his endeavour to climb the hill»? | colour | paper | *attempt | sleep
